{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (an automated orchestrator) has assigned task #5659: implement `cmd/pr/main.go` for the GNU `pr` utility. The task specifically requires implementing SRD requirements R3.1 (multi-column output), R4.1 (line numbering), R4.2 (indentation and page width), and R4.3 (double-spacing and column separator). However, to produce a working binary, the full SRD requirements R1 (page layout), R2 (page options), and R5 (exit codes/SIGPIPE) must also be implemented as foundational infrastructure. The acceptance criteria require: compilation without errors, go vet passing, and satisfaction of each requirement's acceptance criteria from srd110-pr.yaml.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU `pr` utility: paginates/columnates text files for printing\n   - Page layout: 66 lines default (5 header, 56 body, 5 footer), header shows date/filename/page number\n   - Multi-column output: -COLUMN or --columns=COLUMN, fill-down by default, -a fills across\n   - Line numbering: -n[CHAR[WIDTH]], default tab separator, default width 5\n   - Indentation: -o MARGIN for left indent, -w WIDTH for page width (default 72)\n   - Double-spacing: -d flag\n   - Column separator: -s CHAR (default tab)\n   - Page options: -l N (page length), -h HEADER (custom header), -t (omit header/footer), -T (omit pagination)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - Differential testing pattern against `gpr` (Homebrew GNU pr)\n   - Non-goal: -m (merge files side by side) is NOT to be implemented\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max per function (E8)\n   - File size limit: 500 lines per Go source file (E9)\n   - No git commands allowed\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd110-pr.y